<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Kalgold in maiden yr loss, plans shr issue.</title>
<headline>Kalgold in maiden yr loss, plans shr issue.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-03-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended Dec 31, 1996</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Year loss		 9.75</p>
<p>    Working loss	    16.43</p>
<p>    Finance costs	   1.82</p>
<p>    Profit on disposal    8.61</p>
<p>    Turnover		  9.75</p>
<p>Full name: Kalahari Goldridge Mining Co Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - The firm was listed on the Johannesburg Stock Exchange on October 14, 1996 by the issue of Kalahari Goldridge shares as a dividend in specie to shareholders in West Rand Consolidated Mines Ltd (WR Cons).</p>
<p>Directors said they intended to hold a capital raising exercise to raise funds for Phase II of the firm's mining and metallurgical operations on its existing lease area and for further exploration development in the area.</p>
<p>They planned to raise funds by issuing new shares for cash. Monies would be used to buy certain gold prospecting rights totalling over 150,000 hectares in Kalgold's North West lease area from parent (WR Cons) for around four million rand.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
